error[trioxide(wasm-ineligible)]: `norm` is forced into WASM but can't be compiled: constructs `Vec2`, which may run before the class declaration (JS would throw): code runs before it in its module, or the module is in an import cycle
  --> input.ts:4:13 `new Vec2(x, y)`
      `norm` constructs `Vec2`, which may run before the class declaration (JS would throw): code runs before it in its module, or the module is in an import cycle
  help: only numbers, booleans, typed arrays, `number[]`, plain-data objects, local control flow, arithmetic, `Math.*` and calls to other compilable functions can be compiled (docs/PLAN.md §5); remove the directive to keep it in JS
